{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And all that he had he gave into his hand</b> — to be officer and overseer over all that he had, in the house and in the field. And our Rabbis made a midrash of it (Genesis Rabbah 86), they said: he would whisper and enter, whisper and go out. He said to him, \"Mix hot drinks\" — and they were hot; \"Mix lukewarm drinks\" — and they were lukewarm. What is Joseph? Straw in Ephraim, magicians in Egypt — how far? Until he saw the Shekhinah standing above him, as it is written: \"and his master saw that YHWH was with him\" (Genesis 39:3). And the matter is that because his master was an Egyptian who did not know HaShem, they said that upon seeing his great success, he suspected it was by way of sorcery, as is common among the people of his land, until he saw that it was from the Most High in a vision that appeared to him in a dream or while awake in a pillar of cloud and similar things, for the glory of the righteous."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "The midrashic phrase 'מה יוסף, תבן בעפרים, חרשין במצרים' is cryptic in the original and rendered hyper-literally; its precise midrashic sense is deliberately left unresolved."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:22:16.712358018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}